  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.17 - a decode capture that cannot be built no longer kills generation. WebGPUDecodeCapture.TryCaptureAsync THREW on a structural parity mismatch between its two probe captures, while its caller already handled null correctly (decode directly, stop attempting capture for the session). A capture is an optimisation, and an optimisation that cannot be built must never be load-bearing - this turned \"this graph cannot be accelerated\" into \"chat does not work at all\", with the user seeing only 'Error: /api/chat: decode capture parity mismatch'. The mismatch is still reported loudly with its counts, and the untrustworthy diff is still never replayed; only the throw is gone.",
